{{Japanese name|Nakayama}}

'''Rento Nakayama''' (中山 廉斗, ''Nakayama Rento'', born April 12, 1993) is an [[Okaiken|Sanese]] politician, former actor, and social media personality who is the current [[Minister of Health and Welfare of Okaiken|Minister of Health and Welfare]] and leader of the [[Okaiken Socialist Party|Okaiken Socialist Party (OSP)]]. He became a national figure during the [[Okaiken general election, 2025|2025 general election]], where he led the near-extinct OSP from 2 seats to 50 in a populist surge known as "Nakayama-mania."

==Early life and education==
Rento Nakayama was born on April 12, 1993, in Okami, Okaiken. Unlike many in Okaiken's political class, he does not come from a political dynasty; his father was a factory worker and his mother was a nurse. This working-class background became a cornerstone of his political identity. He attended the Okami University of Arts, graduating in 2015 with a degree in performing arts. He later earned a certification in sports nutrition from the Okaiken Sports Science University in 2018.

==Entertainment and fitness career==

===Bodybuilding and fitness===
[[File:Rento Nakayama Competing in Physique Class.png|thumb|left|200px|Rento Nakayama competing for men's physique bodybuilding, 2021.]]
During his university years, Nakayama began dedicated bodybuilding training. For him, it was an exercise in control and self-creation; coming from a world with little economic power, his physique was the one thing he could build and perfect through "pure, scientific discipline."

After graduating, he launched "Ren-Fit," a social media brand that combined his acting charisma with his bodybuilding knowledge. His brand was not about elite-level competition; it was about "democratizing wellness." He became famous for posting videos on how to eat healthy on a minimal budget and for destigmatizing mental health struggles, which he tied to a "sick" society that values profit over well-being.

His brand's slogan—"Build your best self to fight for a better world"—blended self-improvement with social grievance and became the model for his later political movement.

